    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d141">

                <pb facs="0408" n="373" sameAs="frus:frus1977-80v29/pg373"/>

                <head>141. Letter From President Carter to Multiple Recipients<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d141-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1978-02-07">February 7, 1978</date>
                    </dateline>
                    <salute>To Cy, Harold, Zbig, Ham, Frank </salute>
                </opener>
                <p>In my calls &amp; meetings with Senators I’ve found that we are being hurt by
                    varying answers to canal maintenance and operations cost questions.</p>
                <p>Please consult immediately &amp; evolve a clear procedure for answering new
                    questions and for giving to me &amp; others existing and future information.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Jimmy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d141-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d141-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Carter Library, Office of the Chief of Staff, Hamilton Jordan’s
                    Confidential Files, Box 36, Panama Canal Treaty 1978. No classification marking.
                    Sent to Vance, Brown, Brzezinski, Jordan, and Moore.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
